  "content": "[Intro]\n[Bm/F#]\n[Bmadd11/F#]\n[F#7sus4]\n[F#7]\n[A/F#]\n[Em/F#]\n[G6]\n[F#7]\n[Bsus4]\n[B]\n[Bsus4]\n[B]\n[Bsus4]\n[B]\n[E5/B]\n[B]Ever\n\n[Verse 1]\n[E5/B]since I was a young boy, I've\n[B]played the silver ball. From\n[Bm7/A]Soho down to Brighton I\n[Aadd9]must have played them all. But I\n[Gadd11]ain't seen nothing like him In\n[G]any amusement hall... That\n[Bsus4/F#]deaf, dumb and blind kid\nSure plays a mean pin-\n\n[Chorus]\n[B]ball! [A][D]\n[E]\n[B]  [A]  [D]\n[E]He\n\n[Verse 2]\n[E5/B]stands like a statue, Becomes\n[B]part of the machine.\n[Bm7/A]Feeling all the bumpers\n[Aadd9]Always playing clean.\n[Gadd11]He plays by intuition, The\n[G]digit counters fall. That\n[Bsus4/F#]deaf, dumb and blind kid\nSure plays a mean pin-\n\n[Chorus]\n[B]ball! [A][D]\n[E]\n[B]  [A]  [D]\n[E]He's a\n[E]pinball [B][F#7]wizard There [E]has\n[F#7]to be a [B]twist. [E]A\n[F#7]pinball [B]wizard's got [E]\n[G]such a supple\n[D]wrist.\n\n[Interlude]\n[D5]How do you [D5/C]think [Bm7]he [Gsus2]does\n[D5]it? I [D5/C]don't [Bm7]know! [Gsus2]\n[D5]What makes [D5/C]him [Bm7]so [Gsus2]\n[D]good?' He\n\n[Verse 3]\n[E5/B]ain't got no distractions Can't\n[B]hear no buzzers and bells, Don't\n[Bm7/A]see no lights aflashin'\n[Aadd9]Plays by sense of smell.\n[Gadd11]Always gets a replay,\n[G]Never seen him fall. That\n[Bsus4/F#]deaf, dumb and blind kid\nSure plays a mean pin-\n\n[Chorus]\n[B]ball! [A][D]\n[E]\n[B]  [A]  [D]\n[E]I\n[E]thought I [F#7]was [B][E]The\n[F#7]Bally table [B]king [E]But\nI [F#7]just [B]handed my [E]\n[G]pinball crown to\n[D]him\n\n[Bridge]\n[Dsus4]\n[D]\n[Dsus4]\n[D]\n[Dsus4]\n[D]\n[Dsus4]\n[D]Even\n\n[Verse 4]\n[Dsus4]on my favorite table\n[D]He can beat my best. His di-\n[Csus4]sciples lead him in And\n[C]he just does the rest. He's got\n[A#sus4]crazy flipper fingers\n[A#]Never seen him fall... That\n[Asus4]deaf, dumb and blind kid\n[A]Sure plays a mean pin-\n\n[Outro]\n[D]ball! [C][F]\n[A#]",
